o ordain things both great and small, who met rewards and punishments for good and bad acts, and who himself has conquered the three worlds? Resorting* to what other means shall Rāvana secure (victory)? *Explains the commentator: \"Time has every thing under its control. Like the all-enclosing space, time pervades all that is. This being so, resorting what transcending Time, shall Rāvana obtain victory over it.\"","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.525,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-20-26"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7020024","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"907e4b8508ce1bfefb8607854d8418f7aa02efb17371ee9e19e3511b016eae1e","compact":"233126db76e90ed10e5eb492ede1f255e09f7284cbfe4e47aa67141fd36fb1aa","nasal":"233126db76e90ed10e5eb492ede1f255e09f7284cbfe4e47aa67141fd36fb1aa"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-20-25","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":20,"verse":25,"english":"How can (Rāvana) subdue him who ordain things both great and small, who met rewards and punishments for good and bad acts, and who himself has conquered the three worlds? Resorting* to what other means shall Rāvana secure (victory)? *Explains the commentator: \"Time has every thing under its control. Like the all-enclosing space, time pervades all that is. This being so, resorting what transcending Time, shall Rāvana obtain victory over it.\" I am curious about it. To Yama's abode shall I go for witnessing the encounter between Yama and the Raksasa.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.322,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-20-26","DUTT-7-20-27"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7020025","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b3d0439ab8c6ccc17a9ae284e506ff7ae18dab2112ad851601e7d311863cb990","compact":"fca225bdd7177bb53300f28b055fdd63816e6d6e3aba44c3f9fd058f3b21fe32","nasal":"385e01e7c2ba8a2